statement:
Let $m$ be a CNF formula over natural-number variables, let $	au$ be a Boolean assignment satisfying $m$, and let $j,i	ext{ be natural numbers}$ and $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ be another Boolean assignment. If $	au$ and $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ agree at every variable with index less than $i$, and the variable count of $m$ is at most $i+j$, then the prefix of $j$ existential quantifiers starting at index $i$ is true under $	ext{ let }
\sigma$.
